hermes v0.23.0 (+ hermes-vault-payment-iframe-fill.patch): hosted card
fields on a plugin page backend (Camofox), Square, grouped-number redaction.

Symptom: #136981 reaches card frames only over a CDP supervisor; on a
plugin page backend (Camofox, which hyperhermes agents browse with: no CDP)
_payment_frames returns [] and frame writes are refused, so the agent
still cannot pay. Square's Web Payments SDK frame (web.squarecdn.com) and
Adyen's regional live hosts are not in the processor list. A card field
shows the number grouped ("4242 4242 4242 4242"), which the exact-value
redaction of a later browser result read does not catch.

Fix:
- BrowserPageBackend gets two optional methods: child_frames(task_id)
  (direct children of the page only; default none) and
  evaluate_in_frame(task_id, frame_id, expression, secret=...), with the
  same transport rules as evaluate. The vault lists a plugin page's frames
  through them and runs the frame inspection and the fill there; the
  secret path gets the same in-page try/catch and fixed failure text as
  _page_eval. Frame selection is unchanged: the origin and
  ancestorOrigins read inside the frame decide, and the write re-checks.
  The Camofox side is pkgs/hermes-camofox-plugin/vault-frames.patch plus
  pkgs/camofox-browser/vault-frames-plugin.
- PAYMENT_FRAME_ORIGINS adds https://web.squarecdn.com,
  https://sandbox.web.squarecdn.com and checkoutshopper-live-{us,au,apse,in}.adyen.com.
- A card fill also registers the number's grouped forms (4-4-4-4 and Amex
  4-6-5, spaces or dashes) with the redaction boundary.

Not upstream yet (to propose on #136981 / #140788).

